  "problem": "The following table shows some values of a continuous function $f(x)$ over the interval $[-3,5].$\n\n| $x$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $2$ | $4$ | $3$ |\n\nUse the left Riemann sum, with the four subintervals indicated by the data, to approximate the area under the curve $y=f(x)$ over the interval $[-3,5].$",
